Synthesized e-commerce project requirements and actionable development roadmap
Synthesized e-commerce project requirements and actionable development roadmap
Bhai clear ho gaya — Roopesh dada ne next project assign kar diya hai! 😄

Task Summary:

Project: Mini E-commerce Platform (.NET Core)

App 1 — Customer Application:

Registration page — fields: full name, mobile, email, sex, address
Login/Logout — session based
Product listing page
Category page
Add to cart
Payment page
App 2 — Admin/Operations Application:

Same login/logout
Add product page
Add category page
Yeh data DB mein jaata hai → customer app usko fetch karke dikhata hai
Tech requirements:

.NET Core ✅ (dada ne confirm kiya)
Frontend — "Normal chalega" (matlab basic Razor views, fancy nahi chahiye)
Entity Framework + SQL
Baad mein host karna hai (free hosting pe)
Phir same Angular + Web API mein bhi try karna
Timeline: 2 weeks max ⏰

Suggested approach — break into pieces:

Days	Task
1-2	DB design — Users, Products, Categories, Orders, Cart tables
3-5	Customer app — Register/Login/Logout
6-8	Product + Category listing, Add to Cart
9-10	Payment page (dummy/fake gateway)
11-13	Admin app — Add Product/Category
14	Testing + Git push + hosting
Bhai sabse pehle DB schema design kar — Users, Products, Categories, Cart, Orders tables ka structure batau? 🙂

Ha

Jun 14

Architected database schema for e-commerce platform
Architected database schema for e-commerce platform
Bhai chalo DB schema design karte hain — simple but complete! 😄

1. Users Table

sql
CREATE TABLE Users (
    UserId INT PRIMARY KEY IDENTITY(1,1),
    FullName VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    Email VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    Mobile VARCHAR(15) NOT NULL,
    Password VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,  -- hashed
    Sex VARCHAR(10),
    Address VARCHAR(255),
    Role VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'Customer',  -- Customer / Admin
    CreatedDate DATETIME DEFAULT GETDATE()
)
2. Categories Table

sql
CREATE TABLE Categories (
    CategoryId INT PRIMARY KEY IDENTITY(1,1),
    CategoryName VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    Description VARCHAR(255)
)
3. Products Table

sql
CREATE TABLE Products (
    ProductId INT PRIMARY KEY IDENTITY(1,1),
    ProductName VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL,
    Description VARCHAR(500),
    Price DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL,
    StockQty INT DEFAULT 0,
    CategoryId INT FOREIGN KEY REFERENCES Categories(CategoryId),
    ImageUrl VARCHAR(255),
    CreatedDate DATETIME DEFAULT GETDATE()
)
4. Cart Table

sql
CREATE TABLE Cart (
    CartId INT PRIMARY KEY IDENTITY(1,1),
    UserId INT FOREIGN KEY REFERENCES Users(UserId),
    ProductId INT FOREIGN KEY REFERENCES Products(ProductId),
    Quantity INT DEFAULT 1,
    AddedDate DATETIME DEFAULT GETDATE()
)
5. Orders Table

sql
CREATE TABLE Orders (
    OrderId INT PRIMARY KEY IDENTITY(1,1),
    UserId INT FOREIGN KEY REFERENCES Users(UserId),
    TotalAmount DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL,
    OrderStatus VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'Pending',  -- Pending/Paid/Shipped
    OrderDate DATETIME DEFAULT GETDATE()
)
6. OrderItems Table

sql
CREATE TABLE OrderItems (
    OrderItemId INT PRIMARY KEY IDENTITY(1,1),
    OrderId INT FOREIGN KEY REFERENCES Orders(OrderId),
    ProductId INT FOREIGN KEY REFERENCES Products(ProductId),
    Quantity INT NOT NULL,
    Price DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL  -- price at time of order
)
Relationships:

Users (1) -----> (M) Cart
Users (1) -----> (M) Orders
Orders (1) -----> (M) OrderItems
Categories (1) -----> (M) Products
Products (1) -----> (M) Cart / OrderItems
Approach:

Customer App → access: Users, Products, Categories (read), Cart, Orders
Admin App → access: Products, Categories (CRUD)
Bhai yeh schema solid hai 2-week project ke liye.

