Jun 17
Bhai yeh tera default appsettings.json hai — ConnectionStrings section abhi missing hai. Add karte hain! 😄

Updated appsettings.json:

json
{
  "Logging": {
    "LogLevel": {
      "Default": "Information",
      "Microsoft.AspNetCore": "Warning"
    }
  },
  "AllowedHosts": "*",
  "ConnectionStrings": {
    "DefaultConnection": "Server=YOUR_SERVER_NAME;Database=ECommerceDB;Trusted_Connection=True;TrustServerCertificate=True;"
  }
}
Bhai YOUR_SERVER_NAME kya dalna hai pata karne ke liye:

SQL Server Management Studio (SSMS) open karo aur dekho server name kya hai. Common values:

(localdb)\MvcMovieContext-1 — agar LocalDB use kar raha hai
(localdb)\\MSSQLLocalDB — default LocalDB
. ya localhost — agar full SQL Server installed hai
DESKTOP-XXXXX\SQLEXPRESS — agar SQL Express hai
Yeh same connection string dono projects (CustomerApp aur AdminApp) ke appsettings.json mein dalni hai — kyunki dono same database share karenge.

Tera SQL Server kaunsa hai bhai — LocalDB, SQL Express, ya full SQL Server installed hai? SSMS open karke connect screen mein dekh sakta hai. 🙂

