Jun 17
Bhai sahi pakda — but order yeh hai actually! 😄

EF Core ka flow yeh hota hai (Code-First approach):

1. C# Models banao (User.cs, Product.cs, etc.)
        ↓
2. DbContext banao (jisme saare models register honge)
        ↓
3. Migration command chalao
        ↓
4. Migration database mein tables AUTOMATICALLY create kar deta hai
Matlab tujhe manually SQL Server Management Studio mein tables banane ki zaroorat nahi hai!

EF Core khud tables bana dega based on tere C# classes se — isko Code-First Migration kehte hain.

Toh sequence yeh hai:

Step	Kaam
1	Saare 6 Models banao (User, Category, Product, Cart, Order, OrderItem)
2	DbContext class banao
3	Add-Migration InitialCreate command chalao
4	Update-Database command chalao
5	Tables automatically ban jayenge SQL Server mein! ✅
Bhai pehle saare 6 models bana le (jaisa User.cs banaya), phir DbContext banate hain jo inhe SQL tables se connect karega.

User.cs ban gaya dono projects mein? Baaki 5 models bhi bana de same pattern mein — phir DbContext step pe jaate hain. 🙂

