Jun 17
Bhai dekh, asal mein dono databases ban gaye hain — CustomerDB aur MercatoDB — but tu query mein MercatoDB.dbo.Carts se select kar raha hai jab actual mein MercatoDB ke table mein woh columns nahi hain jo tu likh raha hai.

Wait, ek important cheez notice ki maine —

Tere left side Object Explorer mein 2 alag databases dikh rahi hain:

Customerdb  ← (yeh AdminApp wala hoga shayad)
MercatoDB   ← (yeh CustomerApp/MercatoPro wala)
Yeh problem hai! Tune connection string mein shayad alag database names daal diye dono projects mein — isliye 2 separate databases ban gaye, instead of 1 shared database jaisa plan tha.

Ab actual error ka reason —

Query mein tu likh raha hai column names CartId, UserId etc., but agar case-sensitive collation hai SQL Server mein, ya columns alag naam se bane hain (jaise EF Core kabhi-kabhi plural ya different casing use karta hai).

Pehle yeh check karo bhai:

dbo.Carts table pe right-click → Select Top 1000 Rows kar — usse actual column names dikh jayenge jo EF Core ne generate kiye.

Ya expand kar dbo.Carts table Object Explorer mein, aur Columns folder expand kar — exact naam dikhega.

Bhai dbo.Carts expand kar Object Explorer mein aur columns ke naam bata — pata chal jayega exact mismatch kahan hai. 🙂

1781691329102_image.png
