Jun 17
Bhai dekh — columns ke naam toh exactly same hain jo tune query mein likhe the! ✅

CartId, UserId, ProductId, Quantity, AddedDate
Yeh MercatoDB database mein hai, aur tu MercatoDB.dbo.Carts se hi query kar raha tha. Toh confusion yeh hai —

Maine pehle screenshot mein dekha tha:

Query result mein "Invalid column name" errors aa rahe the, but niche "Query executed successfully" bhi likha tha aur 0 rows aaya tha.

Yeh contradiction hai —

Possible reason: Tune SQLQuery2 tab mein jo query likhi thi, woh shayad purani cached error dikha raha tha jab tune pehli baar likha tha (before tables existed), aur IntelliSense ne red underline kiya tha — but jab actually Execute kiya, woh successful chala aur 0 rows return hue (kyunki Cart table abhi khali hai, koi data nahi dala).

Toh asal mein koi real error nahi hai bhai! 😄

Red squiggly lines = IntelliSense cache issue (refresh nahi hua tha)
Actual execution = successful
0 rows = normal hai, kyunki tune Cart table mein kuch insert nahi kiya abhi tak
Confirm karne ke liye:

Query likh ke phir se Execute (F5 ya green Execute button) dabake check kar — error list clear ho jayega ab IntelliSense refresh hone ke baad.

Bhai tension mat le, database aur tables sahi bane hain — sab on track hai! Ab Registration page banana shuru karte hain? 🙂

