Jun 17
Bhai chal aaj ka kaam ek baar properly recap kar lete hain — taaki samajh mein aaye kya kiya aur kyun kiya. 😄

Day 1 — Foundation Setup (Aaj ka kaam)
1. Solution + 2 Projects Banaye
MercatoPro (Solution)
├── MercatoPro (Customer-facing app)
└── AdminApp (Operations/Admin app)
Kyun: Roopesh dada ne bola tha — real e-commerce mein customer app alag hota hai, internal team ka app alag (jaise Amazon ka seller portal vs customer website).

2. EF Core Packages Install Kiye (dono projects mein)
Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer — Database se connect karne ke liye
Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Tools — Migration commands chalane ke liye
Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design — Design-time tools ke liye
Kyun: Yeh packages na ho toh EF Core kaam nahi karega — yeh bridge hai C# code aur SQL Server ke beech.

3. Connection String Add Ki (appsettings.json mein)
json
"ConnectionStrings": {
  "DefaultConnection": "Server=...;Database=MercatoDB;..."
}
Kyun: Yeh batata hai app ko — kaunsa server, kaunsa database use karna hai.

4. 6 Models Banaye (C# Classes)
User.cs, Category.cs, Product.cs, Cart.cs, Order.cs, OrderItem.cs
Kyun: Yeh classes database tables ka blueprint hain — har property ek column banegi.

5. ApplicationDbContext Banaya
csharp
public DbSet<User> Users { get; set; }
public DbSet<Product> Products { get; set; }
// ...etc
Kyun: Yeh class EF Core ko batati hai — "yeh saare models hain, inhe tables mein convert karo."

6. Program.cs mein DbContext Register Kiya
csharp
builder.Services.AddDbContext<ApplicationDbContext>(options =>
    options.UseSqlServer(...));
Kyun: Yeh app ko batata hai — "jab koi request aaye, DbContext available rakhna for database operations."

7. Migration Banaya — Add-Migration InitialCreate
Kyun: Yeh EF Core ko ek plan banata hai — "Database mein yeh 6 tables banao, yeh columns honge, yeh relationships honge."

8. Database Update Kiya — Update-Database
Kyun: Yeh actual command hai jo SQL Server mein tables physically create karta hai — plan ko reality mein convert karta hai.

Result — Final Output:
✅ MercatoDB database ban gaya
✅ 6 Tables ban gaye — Users, Categories, Products, Carts, Orders, OrderItems
✅ Sabhi Foreign Key relationships automatically set ho gaye

Overall Flow Samajh — (Important concept)
C# Class (Model) 
    ↓
DbContext mein register 
    ↓
Migration banao (plan)
    ↓
Update-Database (execute)
    ↓
SQL Table ban gaya!
Yeh hi hai "Code-First" approach — pehle code likha, database automatically ban gaya. (Iska opposite "Database-First" hota hai, jahan pehle DB banate hain, phir code generate hota hai).

Bhai sahi se samjha aaj ka kaam? Kal Registration page se shuru karenge — woh pehla CRUD operation hoga jisme tu form se data leke database mein save karna seekhega! 💪

