Jun 17
Bhai haan, roz ka kaam Git pe push karna chahiye — yeh good practice hai aur Roopesh dada bhi expect karenge tracking ke liye! 😄

Git Push Steps — Aaj ka kaam
Step 1: Check Status (kya changes hue hain)
Terminal ya Git Bash mein project folder mein jaake:

bash
git status
Step 2: Sab files Add karo
bash
git add .
Step 3: Commit karo (meaningful message ke saath)
bash
git commit -m "Day 1: Setup MercatoPro and AdminApp projects with EF Core, Models, DbContext and initial migration"
Step 4: Push karo GitHub pe
bash
git push origin master
(Agar branch ka naam "main" hai toh git push origin main)

Important — Pehle yeh check kar bhai:
1. .gitignore file hai kya?
Agar nahi hai, toh bin/ aur obj/ folders bhi push ho jayenge jo zaroorat nahi hai (yeh auto-generated files hote hain).

Quick fix — .gitignore file banao project root mein:

bin/
obj/
*.user
.vs/
2. Connection String mein Password hai kya?
Agar SQL Authentication use kar raha hai (username/password type), toh appsettings.json mein password public GitHub pe jaa sakta hai — security risk!

Agar Windows Authentication (Trusted_Connection=True) use kar raha hai, toh tension nahi — password nahi hota usme.

Bhai pehle bata — Visual Studio se push karega ya terminal/Git Bash se? Aur .gitignore file already hai ya nahi project mein? 🙂

