Real problem yeh hai bhai —

Tu repos folder ke andar multiple projects already track ho rahe the kisi purane Git repo se (root level pe). Jab tune git init kiya tha MercatoPro solution folder mein — shayad woh already ek parent Git repo ke andar tha (~/source/repos), isliye saare sibling folders bhi commit ho gaye!

Solution — Sabse Pehle Yeh Check Karo:

bash
cd ~/source/repos
git status
Agar yahan bhi "On branch master" dikhe — matlab repos folder root mein hi .git hai, jo problem hai. MercatoPro alag se chahiye tha.

Fix Karne Ka Sahi Tarika:

Step 1: Check karo kahan .git folder hai:

bash
cd ~/source/repos
ls -la
Agar .git dikhe repos folder mein (na ki MercatoPro ke andar), toh yeh confirm hai problem.

Step 2: Sahi Jagah Pe Git Init Karo

bash
cd ~/source/repos/MercatoPro
rm -rf .git
git init
(Yeh sirf MercatoPro folder ke andar naya clean Git repo banayega, baaki sab touch nahi karega)

Step 3: Phir Se Add + Commit + Push

bash
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit MercatoPro"
git remote add origin https://github.com/GauravTelange/MercatoEcommerce.git
git branch -M master
git push -u origin master
Bhai pehle cd ~/source/repos karke ls -la chala — check karte hain .git folder kahan hai exactly. Output bhej de. 🙂

