Bhai mast! 😄 Ab Add.cshtml banate hain — yeh thoda special hai kyunki Category dropdown chahiye.

Pehle samajh — Category dropdown kaise aayega:

Product form mein user ko Category select karna hai dropdown se (jaise "Electronics", "Clothing" etc.) — but woh data Categories table se aana chahiye, na ki hardcoded.

Step 1: Controller mein Add() GET method update karo

csharp
public IActionResult Add()
{
    ViewBag.Categories = _context.Categories.ToList();
    return View();
}
Kyun: ViewBag ek temporary container hai jo Controller se View tak data bhejta hai (DbContext View mein directly access nahi hota).

Step 2: Add.cshtml banao — tu khud try kar

Normal fields (ProductName, Description, Price, StockQty) — Category.cs ke Add.cshtml jaisa pattern follow kar.

Category Dropdown ke liye yeh special syntax use karna:

html
<select asp-for="CategoryId" class="form-control">
    <option value="">Select Category</option>
    @foreach (var cat in ViewBag.Categories)
    {
        <option value="@cat.CategoryId">@cat.CategoryName</option>
    }
</select>
Bhai pehle Controller update kar (ViewBag.Categories add kar), phir Add.cshtml try kar likhne — baaki saare fields tu jaanta hai pattern! 💪

