Bhai agar same page pe wapas aaya (URL change nahi hua, list pe redirect nahi hua) — iska matlab ModelState.IsValid false hai, validation fail ho rahi hai silently.

Reason samajh:

Tere Product.cs model mein navigation property hai:

csharp
public Category Category { get; set; }
Jab form submit hota hai, Category object null hota hai (sirf CategoryId aata hai form se), aur agar Category property pe [Required] jaisa kuch laga hai (ya EF Core implicitly require kar raha hai), toh validation fail ho jaati hai silently.

Fix — Controller ke POST method mein yeh add karo (debug ke liye):

csharp
[HttpPost]
public IActionResult Add(Product product)
{
    ModelState.Remove("Category");   // YEH LINE ADD KARO

    if (ModelState.IsValid)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        _context.SaveChanges();
        return RedirectToAction("Index");
    }

    ViewBag.Categories = _context.Categories.ToList();
    return View(product);
}
Kyun: ModelState.Remove("Category") Razor ko bolta hai — "Category navigation property ko validate mat karo, sirf CategoryId chahiye."

Bhai yeh line add kar, phir dubara try kar submit karna. 🙂

