Bhai bilkul sahi pakda — issue yahi hai! 😄

Tune Add.cshtml form mein ImageUrl field nahi rakha (sahi kiya, kyunki image upload feature baad mein banayenge), but Product.cs model mein ImageUrl ek normal string hai — aur C#/ASP.NET Core mein non-nullable string by default "required" maana jata hai server-side validation mein.

Toh simple matlab:

Form mein field nahi hai → koi value submit nahi hoti → ImageUrl null aata hai
Model expects non-null value (kyunki string hai, string? nahi) → validation fail
Fix — sirf model mein ? lagana hai (jo maine upar bataya):

csharp
public string? ImageUrl { get; set; }
Yeh batata hai C# ko — "ImageUrl optional hai, null ho sakta hai abhi."

Baad mein jab image upload feature banayenge (jaisa humne pehle discuss kiya tha — file upload karke wwwroot/images mein save karna, path ImageUrl mein daalna), tab bhi yeh ? waala model kaam karega — bas controller mein code likhenge jo image save karke path assign karega.

Bhai ? laga de ImageUrl, Description, aur Category ke aage jaisa maine bataya — phir try kar submit karna. Confirm ho jayega ab! 🙂


An unhandled exception occurred while processing the request. SqlException: Cannot insert the value NULL into column 'ImageUrl', table 'MercatoDB.dbo.Products'; column does not allow nulls. INSERT fails. Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.SqlConnection.OnError(SqlException exception, bool breakConnection, A

