Jun 21
Bhai next layer ka issue! 😄 C# model level pe toh fix ho gaya, but database table mein abhi bhi ImageUrl column "NOT NULL" hai (kyunki migration purane model se bani thi, jab ImageUrl required tha).

Reason samajh:

Cannot insert the value NULL into column 'ImageUrl'... column does not allow nulls
Matlab SQL Server table mein ImageUrl column abhi bhi NOT NULL constraint ke saath hai. Sirf C# model change karne se database automatically update nahi hota — naya migration chalana padega.

Fix — Naya Migration Banao
Package Manager Console mein (Default project = MercatoPro ya AdminApp, jahan se migration manage karte the):

bash
Add-Migration MakeImageUrlNullable
Phir:

bash
Update-Database
Yeh kya karega:

EF Core dekhega ki tune model mein ImageUrl ko string? bana diya hai, aur database column ko bhi NULL allow karne ke liye alter kar dega.

Important — dono projects mein same model change kiya tha?

Agar dono (AdminApp aur MercatoPro) ka apna-apna DbContext aur model hai par same database (MercatoDB) use kar rahe hain — toh migration kisi ek se bhi chalega kaam karega, kyunki database ek hi hai.

