Jun 21
Bhai nahi nahi — naya category add karne ki zaroorat nahi hai! 😄

Yeh matlab tha alag cheez — explain karta hoon:

Problem yeh hai:

Product table mein "Category" column sirf number dikha raha hai (1), jabki "Electronics" naam dikhna chahiye — taaki readable/professional lage.

Abhi:        Category: 1
Hona chahiye: Category: Electronics
Yeh data ka problem nahi hai — yeh display/view ka problem hai.

Product.cs model mein CategoryId (number) store hota hai database mein — yeh sahi hai, normal hai. Real-world apps mein bhi ID hi store hoti hai.

But jab list dikhate hain, hume CategoryId ki jagah uska "Name" dikhana chahiye — iske liye Index.cshtml mein chhota sa change karna hoga.

Fix — ProductController.cs ke Index() method mein Include use karo:

csharp
public IActionResult Index()
{
    var products = _context.Products.Include(p => p.Category).ToList();
    return View(products);
}
Include(p => p.Category) — yeh EF Core ko bolta hai "Category ka pura data bhi saath le aao, sirf ID nahi."

Phir Index.cshtml mein change karo:

html
<td>@product.CategoryId</td>
Isko yeh banao:

html
<td>@product.Category.CategoryName</td>
Bhai yeh chhota sa fix hai — naya category nahi banani, bas existing data ko sahi tarike se dikhana hai. Karna chahta hai abhi, ya Day 4 complete maan ke aage badhe? 🙂

