Bhai chalo Day 6 shuru karte hain! 😄

Day 6 — Add to Cart
Goal: Customer product card pe "Add to Cart" button dabaye, woh Cart table mein save ho jaye database mein, user ke saath linked.

Concept Samajh Pehle
Yaad kar tera Cart.cs model:

csharp
public class Cart
{
    public int CartId { get; set; }
    public int UserId { get; set; }
    public User User { get; set; }
    public int ProductId { get; set; }
    public Product Product { get; set; }
    public int Quantity { get; set; }
    public DateTime AddedDate { get; set; }
}
Flow yeh hoga:

Customer Login hai (Session mein UserId stored hai)
        ↓
"Add to Cart" button dabaya kisi Product pe
        ↓
Controller ko pata chalta hai — KAUNSA user, KAUNSA product
        ↓
Cart table mein naya row insert hota hai
Step 1: CartController Banao
MercatoPro → Controllers → Add → Controller → MVC Controller - Empty → naam: CartController

Tu khud try kar — concept samajh:

csharp
using MercatoPro.Models;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;

namespace MercatoPro.Controllers
{
    public class CartController : Controller
    {
        private readonly ApplicationDbContext _context;

        public CartController(ApplicationDbContext context)
        {
            _context = context;
        }

        [HttpPost]
        public IActionResult AddToCart(int productId)
        {
            int? userId = HttpContext.Session.GetInt32("UserId");

            if (userId == null)
            {
                return RedirectToAction("Login", "Account");
            }

            var cartItem = new Cart
            {
                UserId = userId.Value,
                ProductId = productId,
                Quantity = 1
            };

            _context.Carts.Add(cartItem);
            _context.SaveChanges();

            return RedirectToAction("Index", "Product");
        }
    }
}
Samajh:

Line	Kaam
HttpContext.Session.GetInt32("UserId")	Login ke time jo UserId session mein save kiya tha, woh nikal raha hai
if (userId == null)	Agar koi login nahi hai, Login page bhej do
new Cart { ... }	Naya Cart row banaya — current user + selected product
_context.Carts.Add()	Database mein save karne ki taiyari
Bhai yeh Controller bana le — phir Product Index.cshtml mein "Add to Cart" button add karenge har card mein! 🙂

using MercatoPro.Models;

using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;

namespace MercatoPro.Controllers

{

    public class CartController : Controller

    {

        private readonly ApplicationDbContext _context;

        public CartController(ApplicationDbContext context)

        {

            _context = context;

        }

        [HttpPost]

        public IActionResult AddToCart(int productId)

        {

            int? userId = HttpContext.Session.GetInt32("userId");

            if (userId == null) {

                return RedirectToAction("Login", "Account");

            }

            var cartItem = new Cart

            {

                UserId = userId.Value,

                ProductId = productId,

                Quantity = 1

            };

            _context.Carts.Add(cartItem);

            _context.SaveChanges();

            return RedirectToAction("Index","Product");

        }

    }

}

