Day 7 — Cart Page (View + Manage)
Goal: Customer apna cart dekhe — kaunse products add kiye hain, quantity, total price — aur remove bhi kar sake.

Concept Samajh Pehle
Cart page mein yeh dikhana hai:

Product Name | Price | Quantity | Subtotal | Remove Button
-----------------------------------------------------------
Realme Earbuds | ₹1999 | 1 | ₹1999 | [Remove]
Vivo T1 5g | ₹19999 | 1 | ₹19999 | [Remove]
-----------------------------------------------------------
                              Total: ₹21998
Step 1: CartController mein Index() method add karo
Concept:

Session se UserId nikalo
Us user ke saare cart items nikalo database se
Product details bhi saath mein chahiye (Include use karna hoga)
Tu khud try kar — hint:

csharp
public IActionResult Index()
{
    int? userId = HttpContext.Session.GetInt32("UserId");

    if (userId == null)
    {
        return RedirectToAction("Login", "Account");
    }

    var cartItems = _context.Carts
        .Include(c => c.Product)
        .Where(c => c.UserId == userId.Value)
        .ToList();

    return View(cartItems);
}
Samajh:

Line	Kaam
GetInt32("UserId")	Session se current user ka ID nikala
.Include(c => c.Product)	Cart ke saath Product details bhi lao
.Where(c => c.UserId == userId.Value)	Sirf is user ke cart items nikalo
return View(cartItems)	List view ko bhejo
Bhai yeh Index() method CartController mein add kar (AddToCart ke neeche) — phir Index.cshtml banayenge Cart ke liye! 🙂

