Day 9 — Order History Page
Goal: Customer apne past orders dekh sake — kaunse orders place kiye, kab, kitna total, status kya hai.

Concept Samajh Pehle
Customer Login → "My Orders" page →
Sirf us user ke orders dikhenge →
Har order mein OrderItems bhi dikhenge
Step 1: OrderController mein MyOrders() method add karo
Tu khud try kar — hint:

csharp
public IActionResult MyOrders()
{
    int? userId = HttpContext.Session.GetInt32("UserId");

    if (userId == null)
        return RedirectToAction("Login", "Account");

    var orders = _context.Orders
        .Include(o => o.OrderItems)
        .ThenInclude(oi => oi.Product)
        .Where(o => o.UserId == userId.Value)
        .ToList();

    return View(orders);
}
Samajh:

Line	Kaam
.Include(o => o.OrderItems)	Order ke saath OrderItems bhi lao
.ThenInclude(oi => oi.Product)	OrderItems ke saath Product details bhi
.Where(o => o.UserId == userId.Value)	Sirf is user ke orders
Bhai yeh method OrderController mein add kar — phir MyOrders.cshtml banayenge! 🙂

